messages:
sam_sales: FYI Sara's exec demo stalled — embedded webview shows streaming parse errors and disconnects around 35-50s. They want a fast mitigation before tomorrow.
eli_se: Can you drop the client console + a small network snippet? Need to see whether data: lines are being split or truncated.
sara_customer: Pasting client console: "Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input at parseEvent (wv_bridge.js:87)". Network capture shows SSE data payloads that sometimes cut mid-object. Example copy below.
sara_customer: event: message
data: {"id":7,"text":"Intro

"}

event: message
data: {"id":8,"text":"Long paragraph that ge

"}

client attempts JSON.parse on the second data and fails. This is only happening in our iOS webview, desktop is fine.
frank_oncall: Infra: I see a short burst of 429s for that org and several LB resets at the same time. Edge logs: "recv() failed (104): connection reset by peer" and proxy: "upstream timed out (110)". Also a couple of write errors. Could be a brief retry storm + proxy buffering issue that fragments SSE frames.
eli_se: Sounds like two things: (1) the webview's SSE consumer assumes per-data JSON completeness and calls JSON.parse immediately, (2) network closes/buffering can cut data blocks. Short-term we should instruct them to buffer per-event lines and only parse when a full JSON is assembled.
sam_sales: Can we do a one-off infra tweak while they try a shim? Customer wants minimal changes on their side.
frank_oncall: I can apply a temporary throttle for that org to reduce concurrent retries (done) and disable proxy_buffering for streaming routes on canary. Also enabling SSE heartbeat comments every 10s on canary to keep connections alive.
deploy-bot: canary v2.23.0 rolled to us-east-1 at 2123456800
eli_se: Share a tiny non-invasive shim they can inject into the webview runtime (no rebuild) — keeps logic minimal.
sara_customer: Perfect. A tiny shim we can paste into the wrapper would be ideal. Patching the SDK is slower.
eli_se: Snippet to paste into the webview's JS console or inject into runtime: 
```js
// SSE accumulator: tolerates split JSON across multiple data: events
let _acc = '';
function onSseDataLine(line) {
  // line is the string from the event.data payload
  _acc += line;
  try {
    const obj = JSON.parse(_acc);
    handleMessage(obj);
    _acc = '';
  } catch (err) {
    // incomplete — wait for next chunk
    if (_acc.length > 128 * 1024) { _acc = ''; console.warn('dropping oversized partial'); }
  }
}
// optional: flush stale buffer periodically
setInterval(() => { if (_acc) { /* if stuck for >5s, drop */ } }, 5000);
```
Add a small guard so the shim doesn't hold memory indefinitely.
sara_customer: Thanks — we'll inject that now and test. Can you also share any proxy settings we should change?
frank_oncall: On your CDN/proxy, set proxy_buffering off (or equivalent) for the streaming route and increase keepalive_timeout to ~90s. From our side, we disabled buffering on canary and reduced gateway retry concurrency for the org.
eli_se: Also ask them to avoid client-side aggressive retry loops for streaming endpoints — retries can create overlapping connections that confuse proxies and cause resets.
sam_sales: Sara, do you want us to apply the infra throttle now?
sara_customer: Yes please, apply throttle and I'll inject the shim. We'll report back in ~20m. Exec is tomorrow so this is urgent.
frank_oncall: Action list: (1) throttle retries for org (applied), (2) disable proxy_buffering for SSE routes on canary (applied), (3) enable 10s heartbeat comments from canary (in progress), (4) add metric for partial-parse failures (queued). I'll post updates in #eng-runtime if anything changes.
eli_se: For long-term we'll add guidance in the JS SDK and a small helper that robustly handles multi-chunk event payloads and exposes a size/time flush policy.
sam_sales: Thanks team. Marking as POC high-touch. Sara will update once they validate the shim. :thumbsup:
sara_customer: Shim injected, testing now — will update in 18m. Appreciate the quick triage.
